title: Munich in Winter
subtitle: The council republic has lasted a year, and it is hungry.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 1 and bavaria_soviet = 2
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= Munich in Winter

The red flag still flies over the Wittelsbach Palace. Munich and the towns of Upper Bavaria are governed by their councils, and the Red Army holds a front along the Danube and the Lech.

The Hoffmann government in Bamberg blockades the city. The peasants hide their grain, and coal comes in by the wagonload when it comes at all. In the countryside the civil guards drill openly with army rifles. The Executive Council asks the Zentrale what the party will do for it.

- @reinforce: Send cadres, money and rifles to Munich.
- @broaden: Bring the USPD and the peasants' councils into the government.
- @settle: Negotiate a settlement with Berlin.

@reinforce
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Munich becomes a fortress, and the rest of the party goes short.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.bav_strength += 2;
RG.district('bavaria', {loyalty: 10, guards: 2});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our organisers slip across the lines at night with banknotes sewn into their coats.

@broaden
subtitle: Grain from the villages, and a government the party no longer runs alone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.bav_strength += 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 6;
RG.district('bavaria', {members: 0.1});
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

A congress of peasants' councils meets in Freising. Grain starts to come in from a few dozen villages.

@settle
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Autonomy, an amnesty and elections, if the Red Army lays down its guns.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids bargaining with Ebert's government.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.bav_settled = 1;
Q.bav_strength -= 1;
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Through the USPD the Zentrale opens talks with Berlin, and the blockade is lifted while they last. The Red Army hands in its first rifles in February.
